WEBVTT
X-TIMESTAMP-MAP=LOCAL:00:00:00.000,MPEGTS:0

00:00.731 --> 00:03.934 align:center line:79%
While the Savior was traveling
through Bethsaida,

00:03.934 --> 00:06.670 align:center line:79%
some individuals
brought a blind man to Him.

00:06.670 --> 00:10.307 align:center line:79%
Perhaps they were hoping
to see a miracle firsthand.

00:11.308 --> 00:13.810 align:center line:81%
The Savior “took the blind man by the hand

00:14.044 --> 00:17.214 align:center line:79%
and led him out of the town”
to heal him privately.

00:18.148 --> 00:20.851 align:center line:79%
Initially, the healing
seemed less than effective.

00:21.184 --> 00:25.222 align:center line:79%
The blind man “looked up and said,
I see men as trees, walking.”

00:25.889 --> 00:29.927 align:center line:79%
Jesus, compassionately,
“put his hands again

00:29.927 --> 00:32.963 align:center line:81%
upon his eyes, and made him look up.”

00:33.964 --> 00:37.901 align:center line:79%
With that additional touch,
the blind man now “saw ... clearly.”

00:39.136 --> 00:40.804 align:center line:81%
This is just one example

00:40.804 --> 00:45.309 align:center line:79%
of how the Savior's life is characterized
by humble acts of service.

00:46.043 --> 00:51.048 align:center line:79%
He reminds us that He “came not
to be ministered unto, but to minister”

00:51.381 --> 00:56.153 align:center line:79%
and then invites us to follow
His example by going the extra mile,

00:56.486 --> 00:59.790 align:center line:79%
giving to those who ask of us,
and loving our neighbor.

01:00.724 --> 01:02.926 align:center line:81%
When asked, “Who is my neighbor?“,

01:03.393 --> 01:08.632 align:center line:79%
Christ shared the parable of
the good Samaritan with a charge to “go,

01:08.966 --> 01:10.667 align:center line:81%
and do thou likewise.”

01:11.902 --> 01:14.404 align:center line:81%
Missionaries of The Church of Jesus Christ

01:14.404 --> 01:17.274 align:center line:79%
of Latter-day Saints are
modern-day examples

01:17.274 --> 01:20.877 align:center line:79%
of the good Samaritan
that Christ invites us to become.

01:21.812 --> 01:24.047 align:center line:79%
I would like to highlight
those missionaries

01:24.047 --> 01:26.049 align:center line:81%
who are called to service assignments.

01:26.683 --> 01:31.421 align:center line:79%
They are examples to us of how
service (1) open hearts

01:31.421 --> 01:33.190 align:center line:81%
to the gospel of Jesus Christ.

01:33.390 --> 01:37.961 align:center line:79%
(2) allows all of us to minister
regardless of our circumstances,

01:38.195 --> 01:41.965 align:center line:79%
and (3) brings the power
of Christ into our lives.

01:42.766 --> 01:47.037 align:center line:79%
First, service opens hearts
to the gospel of Jesus Christ.

01:47.904 --> 01:52.442 align:center line:79%
In about 91 BC, Ammon,
a Book of Mormon missionary,

01:52.843 --> 01:55.512 align:center line:79%
introduced himself
to King Lamoni by saying,

01:55.946 --> 02:00.517 align:center line:79%
“I desire to dwell among this people for a
time; ... [and] I will be thy servant.”

02:01.652 --> 02:03.987 align:center line:81%
Because of his service to the king,

02:04.021 --> 02:07.157 align:center line:79%
Ammon was granted
an opportunity to “speak boldly, ...

02:07.391 --> 02:11.228 align:center line:79%
and tell [King Lamoni] by what
power” he had performed his service.

02:11.762 --> 02:15.065 align:center line:79%
In return, the king
promised that “whatsoever [Ammon]

02:15.065 --> 02:17.300 align:center line:81%
desirous ... [the king] would grant it.”

02:18.001 --> 02:22.472 align:center line:79%
Ammon's only request was that the king
listened to the message of the gospel

02:22.472 --> 02:24.708 align:center line:81%
of Jesus Christ. Ammon’s

02:24.708 --> 02:27.978 align:center line:79%
service resulted in “thousands
of souls [brought] to repentance.”

02:29.146 --> 02:33.350 align:center line:79%
In our day, service continues
to lead others to the gospel.

02:33.884 --> 02:36.353 align:center line:79%
Sister Bevan was serving
as a teaching missionary

02:36.353 --> 02:40.424 align:center line:79%
when she began experiencing
health issues, requiring requiring her

02:40.424 --> 02:42.025 align:center line:81%
to return home for treatment.

02:42.759 --> 02:44.227 align:center line:81%
Instead of being released,

02:44.227 --> 02:47.931 align:center line:79%
she was able to continue serving
as a service missionary from home.

02:48.832 --> 02:50.067 align:center line:81%
While visiting a park,

02:50.067 --> 02:53.070 align:center line:79%
Sister Bevan and a friend
were prompted to talk to a mother

02:53.070 --> 02:57.507 align:center line:79%
with four young children, but
they hesitated, and the family drove away.

02:58.241 --> 03:00.177 align:center line:81%
The next day, they returned to the park,

03:00.177 --> 03:02.946 align:center line:81%
praying that this family would be there.

03:03.213 --> 03:09.386 align:center line:79%
Miraculously, the mother was sitting
in the exact same spot as the day before.

03:10.053 --> 03:14.324 align:center line:79%
This time, Sister Bevan and her friend
approached the mother, got to know her,

03:14.324 --> 03:17.894 align:center line:79%
and discovered that she was in desperate
need of temporal help.

03:18.628 --> 03:21.098 align:center line:81%
They provided assistance

03:21.098 --> 03:24.367 align:center line:79%
and then invited her to learn
about the gospel.

03:25.502 --> 03:28.472 align:center line:81%
Because of that service and invitation,

03:28.772 --> 03:31.742 align:center line:79%
the mother and her oldest
child were baptized,

03:32.008 --> 03:35.112 align:center line:79%
followed by followed by
the next-oldest a year later.

03:35.445 --> 03:37.314 align:center line:81%
They remain active members today.

03:38.048 --> 03:41.852 align:center line:79%
Sister Bevan knew this experience
was divinely inspired,

03:42.152 --> 03:46.256 align:center line:79%
and it “proved to [her] that [she] was
exactly where God needed [her] to be.”

03:47.491 --> 03:49.426 align:center line:81%
Like Ammon and Sister Bevan,

03:49.626 --> 03:53.630 align:center line:79%
as we serve others,
we “show forth good examples unto them,”

03:53.630 --> 03:56.967 align:center line:79%
and they desire to know the “reason
of the hope that is in [us].”

03:57.567 --> 04:01.805 align:center line:79%
Jesus invites us to “go,
and do thou likewise.”

04:02.873 --> 04:07.744 align:center line:79%
Second, service allows all of us to
minister regardless of our circumstances.

04:08.044 --> 04:11.481 align:center line:79%
President Russell M. Nelson
called on “every worthy,

04:11.515 --> 04:14.785 align:center line:79%
able young man to prepare
for and serve a mission,”

04:15.085 --> 04:17.587 align:center line:81%
and for every able young sister to “pray

04:17.587 --> 04:20.357 align:center line:79%
to know if the Lord
would have [her] serve a mission.”

04:20.357 --> 04:24.261 align:center line:79%
He promised that,
“Your decision to serve a mission,

04:24.261 --> 04:28.799 align:center line:79%
whether a proselyting or a service
mission, will bless you and many others.”

04:28.799 --> 04:34.905 align:center line:79%
Service missions changed
the definition of the word “able.”

04:35.705 --> 04:38.308 align:center line:81%
Now, every worthy young man and woman

04:38.308 --> 04:41.945 align:center line:79%
who desires to serve a full-time
mission for the Lord can do so,

04:41.945 --> 04:43.613 align:center line:81%
with very few exceptions.

04:44.581 --> 04:48.418 align:center line:79%
Elder Holgado is an example
of being able to serve regardless

04:48.418 --> 04:49.953 align:center line:81%
of personal circumstances.

04:50.353 --> 04:52.556 align:center line:81%
He was born with a rare genetic disorder

04:52.556 --> 04:56.193 align:center line:79%
which precluded him from
serving a teaching mission.

04:56.193 --> 04:59.095 align:center line:79%
Elder Holgado was called
as a service missionary

04:59.095 --> 05:01.698 align:center line:79%
and volunteered
in the bishop’s storehouse,

05:01.698 --> 05:04.835 align:center line:79%
where he helped others get
the assistance they needed.

05:04.835 --> 05:07.470 align:center line:81%
He stocked shelves, bagged vegetables,

05:07.470 --> 05:12.242 align:center line:79%
and crushed cardboard boxes. As Elder
Holgado spoke in sacrament meeting

05:12.242 --> 05:17.914 align:center line:79%
after his mission, he shared
that, “God needs service missionaries.

05:18.148 --> 05:20.417 align:center line:81%
He needs people to love and serve others.

05:20.584 --> 05:23.653 align:center line:79%
These people stock
toilet paper, bag broccoli,

05:23.720 --> 05:26.790 align:center line:79%
build furniture, and are good
to people.”

05:27.424 --> 05:31.294 align:center line:79%
You don’t need to have a service
assignment or wear a name tag to do good.

05:31.628 --> 05:34.898 align:center line:79%
Every act of service is
recognized by the Savior.

05:35.232 --> 05:38.401 align:center line:79%
We are all able to help
others come unto Christ by serving

05:38.401 --> 05:39.603 align:center line:81%
with loving kindness.

05:39.870 --> 05:43.240 align:center line:79%
We can all minister in Christ's name
to the one through the power

05:43.240 --> 05:47.744 align:center line:79%
of the Holy Ghost, and live
as examples of faith in Jesus Christ.

05:48.178 --> 05:53.250 align:center line:79%
Service allows us to present ourselves
as living sacrifices

05:53.550 --> 05:55.051 align:center line:81%
who are acceptable to God.

05:56.086 --> 05:59.789 align:center line:79%
Jesus invites us to “go,
and do thou likewise.”

06:00.523 --> 06:04.227 align:center line:79%
Third, service brings the power
of Christ into our lives.

06:04.628 --> 06:07.297 align:center line:79%
A young missionary who transferred
from a teaching assignment

06:07.297 --> 06:08.932 align:center line:81%
to a service assignment struggled

06:08.932 --> 06:13.303 align:center line:79%
with some personal challenges that left
him needing Christ's healing power.

06:13.670 --> 06:16.573 align:center line:79%
Consecrated service
brought that power into his life.

06:16.706 --> 06:19.309 align:center line:79%
He said, “I felt that
when I was struggling,

06:19.309 --> 06:21.177 align:center line:81%
I could feel Christ lifting me up.

06:21.578 --> 06:26.182 align:center line:79%
There is something special about seeing
him bless people through a food pantry,

06:26.182 --> 06:28.485 align:center line:81%
in the temple, and through His gospel.”

06:29.019 --> 06:31.221 align:center line:81%
This elder began to feel deeper joy,

06:31.421 --> 06:35.859 align:center line:79%
and his newfound enthusiasm
blessed him and his entire family.

06:36.293 --> 06:39.062 align:center line:79%
The Spirit entered
their home more abundantly,

06:39.062 --> 06:41.464 align:center line:79%
they attended the temple
together more regularly,

06:41.464 --> 06:44.801 align:center line:79%
and Christ became a greater
focus in their family.

06:45.969 --> 06:49.039 align:center line:79%
This missionary believes
that Christ saved his life

06:49.039 --> 06:51.007 align:center line:81%
and blessed his family through service.

06:51.441 --> 06:54.210 align:center line:79%
President Nelson
taught, “Willingness to serve

06:54.210 --> 06:57.414 align:center line:79%
and strengthen others stands
as a symbol of one's readiness

06:57.447 --> 07:00.483 align:center line:79%
to be healed” by the redemptive
power of the Savior.

07:00.917 --> 07:04.254 align:center line:79%
Christ invites us to “go,
and do thou likewise.”

07:05.322 --> 07:10.160 align:center line:79%
Service missionaries are examples
of consecrated disciples of Jesus Christ.

07:10.593 --> 07:14.397 align:center line:79%
When your family member is blessed
with a call as a service missionary,

07:14.664 --> 07:16.766 align:center line:81%
that is a moment to celebrate.

07:17.267 --> 07:20.103 align:center line:79%
Your family will have a
set-apart representative

07:20.103 --> 07:22.272 align:center line:81%
of Jesus Christ living in your home.

07:22.906 --> 07:26.810 align:center line:79%
That will change all of you for the good.
There should be no disappointment

07:26.810 --> 07:28.211 align:center line:81%
in any call to serve.

07:28.411 --> 07:31.181 align:center line:81%
We sing, “I’ll go where you want me to go”

07:31.481 --> 07:33.249 align:center line:81%
And “I’ll be what you want me to be.”

07:33.750 --> 07:37.320 align:center line:79%
Here is an opportunity to show
that we really mean what we say!

07:38.421 --> 07:40.190 align:center line:81%
To all of you who serve,

07:40.557 --> 07:44.294 align:center line:79%
and especially to the over
four thousand young service missionaries,

07:44.627 --> 07:48.932 align:center line:79%
we love you! If teaching
missionaries are the Lord’s mouth,

07:48.932 --> 07:51.534 align:center line:79%
then service missionaries
are the Lord’s hands,

07:51.534 --> 07:55.338 align:center line:81%
and you are not second-class missionaries.

07:56.306 --> 08:00.443 align:center line:79%
Each of you is vital
to the gathering of Israel.

08:00.910 --> 08:05.715 align:center line:79%
President Nelson taught that “Anytime
we do anything that helps anyone ...

08:05.715 --> 08:10.787 align:center line:79%
to make and keep their covenants with God,
we are helping to gather Israel.”

08:10.787 --> 08:13.923 align:center line:79%
You service missionaries
gather Israel in so many ways,

08:13.923 --> 08:15.959 align:center line:81%
and your service changes lives.

08:16.259 --> 08:21.331 align:center line:79%
Often you don't know who the beneficiary
of your service is, but God knows.

08:21.798 --> 08:25.902 align:center line:79%
Always remember that “inasmuch
as you [serve] one of the least of these,

08:26.202 --> 08:32.275 align:center line:79%
.... ye [serve Him].” We hear your voices
as you volunteer at Church call centers,

08:32.542 --> 08:36.112 align:center line:79%
we see your smiles as you help
in community organizations,

08:36.346 --> 08:39.883 align:center line:79%
and we feel your light
as you serve in temples.

08:40.250 --> 08:44.654 align:center line:79%
You feed the hungry, clothe the naked,
and give drink to the thirsty.

08:45.121 --> 08:48.224 align:center line:81%
We all need to “go, and do ... likewise.”

08:49.059 --> 08:52.762 align:center line:79%
Service is the lifeblood
of disciples of Christ.

08:53.263 --> 08:56.266 align:center line:79%
Service has the power
to open hearts to the gospel

08:56.499 --> 09:00.270 align:center line:79%
and allows all of us
to give our whole soul to Christ.

09:00.703 --> 09:04.641 align:center line:79%
It changes our hearts to become
more like Him, and, in the process,

09:04.641 --> 09:05.842 align:center line:81%
we lift others.

09:06.910 --> 09:11.614 align:center line:79%
President Nelson once asked, “In this
world smitten with spiritual decay,

09:12.048 --> 09:13.883 align:center line:81%
can individuals ... make a difference?”

09:14.150 --> 09:19.522 align:center line:79%
His answer, “Yes! ... ’The covenant people
of the Lord, ... armed ...

09:19.656 --> 09:21.825 align:center line:81%
with the power of God and great glory’ ...

09:22.325 --> 09:26.763 align:center line:79%
can lift the lives of all
humankind.” Through service,

09:27.130 --> 09:29.766 align:center line:81%
we change hearts, and the world.

09:31.067 --> 09:34.104 align:center line:81%
Christ “went about doing good.”

09:35.004 --> 09:38.641 align:center line:79%
He ministered to the sick,
gave sight to the blind,

09:39.476 --> 09:41.244 align:center line:81%
and visited the downtrodden.

09:42.045 --> 09:47.484 align:center line:79%
He cooked meals, helped at wedding feasts,
and fed thousands who were hungry.

09:48.751 --> 09:51.121 align:center line:81%
As we serve in Christ's name to the one,

09:51.621 --> 09:56.292 align:center line:79%
we become increasingly holy and worthy
of the gift of eternal life.

09:56.926 --> 10:01.197 align:center line:79%
Jesus Christ lives.
He is my Savior and yours.

10:01.464 --> 10:05.902 align:center line:79%
He is our Redeemer. He is our great
Example of ministering.

10:06.503 --> 10:10.840 align:center line:79%
I invite each of us to “go,
and do ... likewise.”

10:11.174 --> 10:13.443 align:center line:81%
In the name of Jesus Christ, amen.

